#---
# purpose: "a message no parked receive matches is gifted whole and waits in the receiver's mailbox until a later receive asks for it; each list cell that crosses is copied once, by its sender"
#---
#
# The parent parks on `:go`. The child's first send, `{:other, [7, 8]}`, is
# rejected by the matcher, so the child gifts the whole message and the parent
# stays parked. The second send, `:go`, matches and wakes the parent. The parent
# grafts both gifts at its dispatch: `:go` finishes the first receive and
# `{:other, [7, 8]}` is in the mailbox for the second. The list the parent
# prints was copied by the child and by nobody else: the run's
# `runtime::copy_list_cell` site counts the 2 cells of the child's gift.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  spawn(fn () ->
    send(parent, {:other, [7, 8]})
    send(parent, :go)
  end)
  receive do
    :go -> dbg(:go)
  end
  receive do
    {:other, xs} -> dbg(xs)
  end
end
